ding, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) vs Myelodysplastic Syndrome with Excess Blasts / Therapy-Related AML:\n  Favours first:  autosomal dominant inheritance, somatic mutation\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal circulating albumin concentration, abnormal circulating protein concentration, abnormal mean corpuscular volume, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) vs Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML):\n  Favours first:  acute myeloid leukemia, autosomal dominant inheritance\n  Favours second: abdominal swelling, abnormal basophil morphology, abnormal granulocyte morphology, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues, bleeding easily\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) vs Polycythemia Vera (PV):\n  Favours first:  acute myeloid leukemia, autosomal dominant inheritance, somatic mutation\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal erythrocyte morphology, bleeding gums, blurred vision, bone pain\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) vs Essential Thrombocythemia (ET):\n  Favours first:  acute myeloid leukemia\n  Favours second: abnormal cerebral vascular morphology, abnormal platelet morphology, abnormal thrombocyte morphology, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology, amaurosis fugax\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) vs Primary Myelofibrosis (PMF):\n  Favours first:  acute myeloid leukemia, autosomal dominant inheritance\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal megakaryocyte morphology, abnormal thrombosis, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology"}
